{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794460515,"nonce":"Ua5YFoN7EQWGsOm8ccGXgyTTM7s=","title":"x","message":"Today a library trust grant is keyed by the library's source without its commit (ADR-0076; migration 0095 `library_source_grants`). Once an org grants `registry_credential` (or `forge_credentials`) to `lib:someone/push`, every later commit of that source gets the credential too. A hijacked upstream account or a malicious update inherits the grant without any operator action.\n\nScarab can't stop code holding a working credential from copying it. The grant is the trust decision, so it should cover the code the operator actually reviewed.\n\nProposal:\n- Credential grants (`registry_credential`, `forge_credentials`) are keyed by source plus commit (or library digest). Moving an invoke to a new commit needs the operator to grant again before a Run that uses it is admitted.\n- Grants with no credential (`build_sandbox`, and plain library trust) can stay keyed by source. The owner may want the sandbox grant pinned too.\n- Run admission's refusal names the source, the granted commit and the requested commit, so the fix is obvious.\n- UI: the Libraries page shows the commit each credential grant covers, with a \"grant this commit\" action. Existing source-wide grants need a migration path: keep them as is with a warning, or require a re-grant at the next release.\n\nTrade-off: every library upgrade needs an operator click, which is friction for library users and for the first-party clone and build libraries too (no first-party special case, owner 2026-11-10).\n\nRelated layers, not in this ticket (operator configuration, documented in the ECR page, ace8135 / #183):\n- an `aws:SourceVpce` / `aws:SourceVpc` condition on the push role, so a copied credential fails outside the cluster's VPC;\n- push roles per Environment, limited to named repositories;\n- egress NetworkPolicy for credential Steps.\n\nNeeds an owner decision. It changes the ADR-0076 trust model for every library, not just build.","files":null}]}